      "message": "Messages longer than `CONFIG_SHELL_PRINTF_BUFF_SIZE - 1` will be split into multiple `zephyr_print` calls. Since the shell lock is released between flushes, chunks from concurrent logs can interleave. Is this a known trade-off for avoiding backend locks?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 65,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "eb77413447599e3b87f8105169e001ac172e9ae7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
