      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T10:53:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this is a known issue. The buffer size matches the one from console.c. It is not the pretties solution, but hard to find a better one here. We could just increase the buffer endlessly, which impacts stack usage. Anyway, based on my analysis, all logs fit into the SHELL_PRINTF_BUFF_SIZE size buffer.\n\nAdditionally, adding any type of synchronization mechanism on logging path is tricky, and can introduce more problems. The logging can be called from very different contexts like threads with already locked mutexes/spinlocks, ISRs, crashes etc.",
      "parentUuid": "7e572afb_f22cec67",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 65,
        "endChar": 0
